{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["The Sadducees say that <b>our yield</b> is a proof that the beginning of the year is from Nisan, but this is no proof, for it is possible that the meaning of תבואתנו is what the land produces of itself. And if they say it is not called תבואה but rather aftergrowth (ספיח), behold, against them: מן השדה תאכלו את תבואתה. And further, let them inform us how it is done in the Jubilee year, for they do not sow in the sixth and in the seventh and in the eighth, but they sow in the ninth and reap in the tenth. And why does the verse not mention this, since it speaks only of three years? And the correct interpretation in my eyes regarding ועשת את התבואה is that I will give a blessing in the sixth, that it will suffice and add yet another year, and in the Jubilee year there will be three years without additions."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:21.508182994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}